This file is the per-package legal notice for `@trafilaturacore/launder-replacement`.

It covers only the code in THIS directory. It is NOT, and must never be read as,
a notice for the `launder` package that this module is installed in place of.
No published `launder` release ships a copyright-and-permission notice, and none
may be manufactured on its behalf — that is precisely why this replacement exists.

The directory contains two distinguishable parts, both permissively licensed:

1. The dangerous-href algorithm, ported from `sanitize-html@2.17.3` (`index.js`
   lines 728-768, `naughtyHref`), the last release that carried it inline before
   it was extracted into `launder`. That tarball ships the MIT text reproduced
   below under P'unk Avenue LLC's copyright, and `index.js` carries the same
   notice inline with the exact tarball digest.

2. The `(href, options)` adapter, its option defaults, and the module's own
   arrangement, which are original to this repository.

